rlm-gar-version-rm [-n|--dry-run]

Delete individual versions inside a single Artifact Registry package.
Two pickers: first choose one <repo>/<package>, then TAB-multi-select
the versions (digests) inside it to delete.

Where gar-rm removes a whole package, this prunes selected versions
and leaves the package in place — the tool for dropping old builds
while keeping the current ones.

The package picker is the shared gar-* picker: same cache, same MRU
history, same --- REFRESH CACHE --- partial-refresh flow as gar-open
and gar-rm.

The version picker lists every version newest-first, showing date,
size, short digest, and tags (untagged versions are dimmed). The
preview pane shows the image name, every tag on the digest, the full
SHA, size, media type (flagging multi-arch indexes), upload/update/
create/build times, platform, and any other scalar metadata the API
returns. A digest carrying more than one tag is called out
explicitly, since deleting it removes all of them.

The whole version list is fetched once and handed to the preview as a
cached file, so moving through the list costs no API calls.

DELETION

The exact gcloud command lines are printed before a single
confirmation covering the whole selection. Deletion then runs in
batches of at most 1000 digests — the server rejects a larger single
delete — via:

  gcloud artifacts versions delete <digests…> --package=<pkg>
    --location=<loc> --repository=<repo> --project=<proj>
    --delete-tags --quiet

Version ids are taken from the picker rows, which carry the bare
digest; `versions list --format='value(name)'` returns fully
qualified resource paths that this subcommand rejects when
--package/--location/--repository are given.

Afterwards the package is re-listed and each selected digest checked
against what remains. Any still present are reported and a single
retry offered. Selecting every version in a package deletes the
versions but leaves an empty package behind; that is called out
before you confirm, with a pointer to gar-rm.

OPTIONS
  -n, --dry-run
              Show both pickers, the selection summary, and the exact
              commands, but run no deletes and ask no confirmation.

  -h, --help  Print usage and exit.

ENVIRONMENT
  GAR_SEARCH_PROJECTS
              Colon-separated list of GCP project IDs to browse.
              Required; shared with gar-open, gar-search and gar-rm.

REQUIRES
  gcloud, fzf, jq, curl, python3.

SEE ALSO
  gar-rm      Delete whole packages (all versions plus the package).
  gar-open    Browse packages and open one in the GCP console.
  gar-search  Non-interactive substring search over packages.

NOTE
  OSC 8 hyperlinks in the preview pane require a terminal emulator
  that supports them (Kitty, Ghostty, iTerm2, WezTerm). Inside tmux
  also set: set -ga terminal-features "*:hyperlinks"
